0,Isanzu people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isanzu_people,"The Isanzu have matrilineal descent groups and are agriculturalists who subsist on sorghum, millet, and maize. Most Isanzu make a living as farmers and through migrant labour to other parts of the country, principally, Arusha.",Isanzu,Niger-Congo
1,Isanzu language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isanzu_language,"Isanzu is a Bantu language spoken by the Isanzu people south of Lake Eyasi in Tanzania. The position of Isanzu within the Bantu family is uncertain. It is rather distinct in certain features from other Bantu languages of the area, such as Nyaturu, but is quite close in others.",Isanzu,Niger-Congo
